<title>POLAND: BRE TO ISSUE SHARES FOR COMMERZBANK.</title>
<headline>BRE TO ISSUE SHARES FOR COMMERZBANK.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) wants to issue between 2.5 and 4.5 million shares or convertible bonds for Germany's Commerzbank which now has 31.8 percent in the bank, BRE said in a Thursday statement.  </p>
<p>The issue would be voted on BRE's general shareholders meeting on May 28, the statement said.</p>
<p>It also said that the Polish central bank (NBP) and the Polish Securities Commission (KPW) had not yet approved the issue and Commerzbank taking the shares.</p>
<p>In February, the NBP said that Commerzbank could have up to 32.9 percent of shares in BRE, and since then the German bank increased its stake in BRE to 31.8 percent from 21 percent.</p>
<p>BRE currently has 14.5 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
